The search fence no longer tells the model that a ripgrep config can reshape its output. That has been false since yoagent 0.25.5. It's committed as 2b0e1afd, titled "Part of #1023". The full check (fmt, build, clippy with -D warnings, cargo test) is green: 6622 passed, 0 failed.

What's true now: I read yoagent 0.25.5's tools/search.rs. Its search passes --no-config to rg and removes RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH and GREP_OPTIONS from the child's environment. That applies to rg and to the grep fallback.

What I changed in `src/fence_result_filter.rs`:
• The note the model receives when a line is dropped no longer names a ripgrep config. It now says the line didn't name a file under the searched path, so the fence couldn't check it and dropped it.
• The module doc is in present tense and lists what can still trigger the drop:
  • a file name containing a newline: measured on GNU grep 3.11. d/a\nb.txt comes out as d/a and b.txt:1:tok, and neither line can be traced to a file.
  • a grep that prints its "binary file matches" notice on stdout: older GNU grep (before 3.5) did this, per its release notes.
  • a wrapper `rg` or `grep` on `PATH` that adds its own flags.
  • any output form the parser doesn't recognise.

  The sentence relying on yoagent's --no-config now has a yoagent-version-claim: 0.25.5 marker, so the next upgrade's version check will make someone re-read it.
• The drop itself is unchanged. It stays as a second line of defence.
• New test: unattributed_note_names_no_cause_the_code_cannot_know checks the exact text that comes out of fence_tool_result. It also checks that neither RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH nor ripgrep config appears. It failed against the old note before I rewrote it. No existing test pinned the old text, and I didn't edit any.

ARCHITECTURE.md: in the Day-229 entry I marked "--no-config cannot be added there" as a superseded claim (true until 0.25.5, b58e4329) instead of deleting it. The entry now gives the current reason for dropping lines it can't attribute, and quotes the new note.

Still wrong, left out on purpose: docs/src/configuration/permissions.md:212-215 still tells users that a ripgrep config reshapes fenced search results, and to unset RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH to get dropped matches back. That file was outside this task, so I listed it in the commit body and on #1023 rather than editing it.

Still open on #1023: item 2 (the (N matches) / (N files) footer still shows the pre-filter count after lines are withheld) and item 3 (find/rg warning lines after the footer can name denied paths). I posted the commit, the remaining drop triggers and these open items as a comment on #1023.

